new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:80:    - The visible pattern has horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry on a large lower/right strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:81:    - The top and left outer strips also expose transpose counterparts for cells not recoverable by those reflections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:86:    - For each marker pixel, copy the unique non-marker value in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; if that orbit is entirely hidden in the outer strip, use the transposed top/left-strip counterpart.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:103:            values = _reflection_orbit_values(g, r, c, lo, marker)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:147:    \"\"\"Return the LR+UD reflection orbit of (r, c) within the [_LO.._HI] axes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:224:    \"\"\"Build a clean NxN grid with bilateral LR+UD symmetry on the [lo..N-1] axes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:233:    # Top border rows: LR-symmetric on [lo..N-1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:239:    # Left border cols: UD-symmetric on [lo..N-1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/0934a4d8.py:245:    # Top-left corner: free (no symmetry constraint)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a47bf94d.py:9:_X_OFF = [(-1, -1), (-1, 1), (0, 0), (1, -1), (1, 1)]  # diagonals + center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a47bf94d.py:182:    - bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/db695cfb.py:9:    Connect same-color diagonal pixel pairs, then emit perpendicular rays from differently-colored pixels on those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/db695cfb.py:12:    - bg = most common color. Line color (e.g. blue) has pixel pairs aligned on shared diagonals. Trigger color (e.g. magenta) pixels sit along those diagonals.\n/hom